        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles T. Bernard, J. William Fulbright\n- Roles: Republican nominee, United States Senator\n- Places: Fayetteville, United States\n- Programs: Fulbright Program\n- Concepts: international exchange\n\nFacts:\n- In 1968, Charles T. Bernard was the Republican nominee for the United States Senate seat held by J. William Fulbright.\n- J. William Fulbright was a long-time Democrat from Fayetteville.\n- J. William Fulbright worked to establish an international exchange program.\n- J. William Fulbright’s efforts eventually led to the creation of the fellowship program named after him, the Fulbright Program.",
